The area of the isosceles trapezoid $ABCD$ is equal to the sum of the areas of the triangles $ABC$ and $ADF$:
\[ \frac{1}{2}(AB + CD)(AD) = 25\sqrt{3} + 25\sqrt{3} = 50\sqrt{3} \]

So the area of the shaded region is
\[ \boxed{100\sqrt{3}} \]

