   \begin{align*}
   x &= r \cos \theta \\
   y &= r \sin \theta
   \end{align*}
where $r = 5$ and $\theta = \frac{3\pi}{2}$.

   \begin{align*}
   x &= 5 \cos \left( \frac{3 \pi}{2} \right) \\
   y &= 5 \sin \left( \frac{3 \pi}{2} \right)
   \end{align*}

Since $\cos \left( \frac{3 \pi}{2} \right) = 0$ and $\sin \left( \frac{3 \pi}{2} \right) = -1$, we have:

